// Helper for #1430. Does NOT include func-source.cnx, so `sharedHelper` is
// undefined HERE whichever order the entry lists the includes in.
//
// WHAT THIS PAIR COVERS, and what it does not (#1456). It asserts E0427 fires
// on a cross-file value reference, under both include orders, with two
// controls. It does NOT catch the defect #1430 is named for: restoring the
// `CodeGenState.knownFunctions` read leaves both fixtures GREEN -- measured.
// #1320 hoisted 2.1 Analyze whole-program, so during analysis in a fresh
// process that set is empty and the stale read has nothing stale to return,
// and every fixture runs one program in one process.
//
// The leak that survives is cross-RUN, and
// `src/transpiler/__tests__/CrossRunKnownFunctions.test.ts` is what catches
// it: two runs through one `Transpiler`, mutation-checked, where this pair
// stays green and that one reddens.

u32 localHelper() {
    return 7;
}

// Control, must stay SILENT: localHelper is declared in this very file, so a
// value reference to it is defined, which is all E0427 asks. Without this, a
// fix that rejected every function-as-value would still pass the assertions
// below. It takes the function-body form because that is the spelling that
// also compiles: ADR-029 licenses a function name as a callback TYPE whose
// value is the function, not as an initializer for a u32 -- and the file-scope
// form of even the typed spelling emits a .h/.c pair that disagree about what
// `localHelper` is (#1497, #1498). A test-error fixture never compiles, so a
// control that only transpiles would pin a broken construct unnoticed.
u32 useLocal() {
    localHelper ownLimit <- localHelper;
    return ownLimit();
}

// The defect: declared only in func-source.cnx, which this file does not
// include. Must be rejected under BOTH include orders.
u32 borrowedLimit <- sharedHelper;

// Control, must ALWAYS fire: declared in no file at all. An analyzer that
// stopped firing entirely would silence the line above and still look green
// without this one.
u32 neverLimit <- neverDeclaredAnywhere;
